1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:47,088
Wait.

3
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:48,339
Don't touch me!

4
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:50,550
Don't go.

5
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:55,180
Look.

6
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:58,600
It's fine. Why do you keep running away?

7
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:00,393
Because it's not fine!

8
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:04,481
I could end up killing you,
Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

9
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,401
I don't care anymore.

10
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:09,319
It's just…

11
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,654
Even just looking at you

12
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,199
is scary

13
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:16,534
and painful for me.

14
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:19,579
Please.

15
00:01:21,164 --> 00:01:22,874
Just leave. Please.

16
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,608
-Bo-bae, you're back.
-Come on in.

17
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:51,319
What are you guys doing?

18
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:53,530
I told them. Come sit here.

19
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:58,493
"Triggers for Bo-bae's Powers."

20
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:00,537
"Protocols
for Bo-bae's Electrical Incidents."

21
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:02,122
"Conductive Materials."

22
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:05,166
"Damage Claims and Reimbursement Log."

23
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:07,836
"Bo-bae's Electrical Anomalies."

24
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:16,719
First. "The cockroach incident."

25
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:25,061
A cockroach!

26
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,980
-Ji-hye!
-What's wrong? What happened?

27
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:29,524
A cockroach!
Ji-hye, hurry up and catch it.

28
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:33,153
-Ji-hye!
-Mom!

29
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:36,406
Ji-hye, are you okay?

30
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:38,616
Na Bo-bae is so annoying.

31
00:02:40,702 --> 00:02:42,620
-Mom.
-Hey, just a second!

32
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,126
Bo-bae.

33
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:54,174
"After that, her powers were gone
for an hour and a half."

34
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:56,134
"The first anomaly."

35
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:59,721
Second. The Christmas Santa incident.

36
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:08,813
Santa?

37
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,315
Bo-bae.

38
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:14,360
What? It's you, Dad.

39
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,278
Huh?

40
00:03:16,696 --> 00:03:19,490
No, I'm Santa.

41
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:22,952
It's you, Dad!

42
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:24,412
No, I'm not.

43
00:03:27,207 --> 00:03:29,459
"After that,
her powers were gone for four hours."

44
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:31,628
"Does she lose her powers when startled?"

45
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:36,633
"Or is it because she used
too much of her powers in one go?"

46
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:42,055
One summer, she passed out
while supplying power to a broken AC

47
00:03:42,138 --> 00:03:44,265
and lost her powers for 24 hours.

48
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:48,186
Someone got stuck in the subway doors,
and she fixed them with her powers--

49
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:51,814
Yes, we know. She's been without powers
for up to 48 hours before.

50
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:52,899
That's right.

51
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:56,903
Bo-bae, did you overuse
your electrical powers recently?

52
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:00,281
Recently?

53
00:04:15,838 --> 00:04:18,132
Yeah. I did.

54
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:23,263
I did save someone
who went into cardiac arrest, but…

55
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:24,347
What?

56
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:26,474
Huh?

57
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:31,104
But my powers came back
at Yong-gi's dojo today.

58
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:32,647
What?

59
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:39,153
What's up?

60
00:04:47,787 --> 00:04:48,621
What is it?

61
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:50,873
-Watch your step.
-Okay.

62
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,918
Careful.

63
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,003
Oh dear.

64
00:04:55,628 --> 00:04:56,462
Careful.

65
00:05:00,591 --> 00:05:01,801
The lights are back on.

66
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:03,177
-Oh man.
-Huh?

67
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:04,846
What's this?

68
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:08,182
The building's old.
Sometimes the lights go out on their own.

69
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,600
I have to tap the fuse box.

70
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:12,312
No wonder the rent was so cheap.

71
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:14,689
I told you to do your research
before signing the lease.

72
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:18,276
-The landlord said everything was fixed.
-Hold on.

73
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:19,527
So you're saying

74
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:23,531
the sparks and the lights going out
wasn't because of me?

75
00:05:23,614 --> 00:05:25,867
Oh, no. That happens all the time.

76
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:27,618
-What? All the time?
-Gosh.

77
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,495
When did your powers go away?

78
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:32,707
I'm not sure exactly,

79
00:05:33,624 --> 00:05:35,960
but I noticed it two nights ago.

80
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:38,713
Around 9 p.m.? 9:30?

81
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:41,799
So it's been

82
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:45,803
about 45 hours.

83
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,764
It hasn't been 48 hours yet, right?

84
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:49,724
But the CPR was two weeks ago.

85
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:51,851
Shouldn't we count from then?

86
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:56,481
You said you found out two nights ago.

87
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:59,275
Let's just wait until the 48-hour mark.

88
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:02,403
If your powers aren't back by then,
we'll know for sure.

89
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:04,572
It would be a new record.

90
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:07,700
We'll have to wait
and see if it's really gone, right?

91
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:09,702
For real?

92
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:10,912
That's awesome.

93
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:13,331
-Huh?
-Not again.

94
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,919
-I told you to check everything.
-You had us all confused!

95
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:20,463
Tell the landlord to fix it right away.
Seriously…

96
00:06:20,546 --> 00:06:23,049
Okay, I will.

97
00:06:29,764 --> 00:06:31,849
Even just looking at you is scary

98
00:06:32,392 --> 00:06:34,143
and painful for me.

99
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:35,853
Please.

100
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:39,273
Just leave. Please.

101
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:46,280
Hey, you should've looked into it properly
instead of rushing things.

102
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:47,907
Call the landlord right now.

103
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,742
-I heard you.
-He's just like someone.

104
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:50,952
Exactly the same.

105
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:52,829
-What?
-He takes after me.

106
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:55,081
Take after you? I take after Mom.

107
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:55,998
A cat!

108
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,668
-Over there! A stray cat!
-Is it Gela? My sweet Angela?

109
00:06:58,751 --> 00:06:59,836
-In there.
-Who's Angela?

110
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:01,504
-She's back early.
-Your first love?

111
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:04,674
She's my final love, you punk.
I always feed that cat.

112
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:06,676
Your dad's last first love was…

113
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:08,845
Why are you still here?

114
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:11,431
Quick! Hide!

115
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,272
What if my family sees you?

116
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:21,065
I told you.

117
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:23,651
I feel like I'd die without you.

118
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:27,864
But things are different now.

119
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:29,907
It's not the same anymore.

120
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:33,286
Nothing has changed.

121
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:35,830
If we live together like before
and find a way--

122
00:07:35,913 --> 00:07:36,914
What is this about?

123
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:42,670
You lived together?

124
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:44,630
You mean,

125
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:46,757
under the same roof?

126
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:50,887
Like eating and sleeping together?

127
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,472
Are you two

128
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:54,390
dating?

129
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,142
No, it's not like that.

130
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:57,185
To be precise,

131
00:07:58,102 --> 00:07:59,353
we were officially dating.

132
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:02,982
But when I was unconscious
after nearly dying,

133
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:05,693
Ms. Na Bo-bae

134
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:08,237
abandoned me and ran away.

135
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:11,908
No.

136
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:14,619
You make it sound like
I'm a piece of trash.

137
00:08:16,829 --> 00:08:19,373
That makes me
the father of a piece of trash.

138
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:21,125
Hey.

139
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:23,961
Let's talk inside.

140
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:27,632
Let's go inside. Come on.

141
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:30,885
Come on.

142
00:08:56,285 --> 00:08:57,495
So

143
00:08:57,995 --> 00:09:00,623
you followed Bo-bae here
because you like her?

144
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:03,501
That's what stalkers do.

145
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:06,254
He's been following Bo-bae around
for ages.

146
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:08,798
-He even came to your café, right?
-Hey.

147
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:12,051
He was a very important customer.
Don't talk about him like that.

148
00:09:12,134 --> 00:09:13,427
He's a VIP at my café.

149
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:14,428
What does he do?

150
00:09:14,512 --> 00:09:15,429
I'm…

151
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:19,433
I'm self-employed too.

152
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:21,310
I'm in the lodging business.

153
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:23,187
I see.

154
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:26,691
We moved here after retiring.
Now we grow and sell Shine Muscat grapes.

155
00:09:26,774 --> 00:09:28,693
It's really late now.

156
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:30,736
I told you to leave earlier.

157
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:33,322
What? She told you to leave,
but you didn't listen?

158
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:35,908
Geez, this guy is dangerous.

159
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:37,243
Hold on.

160
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:39,495
He said they dated.

161
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:42,748
Then what about the electrical powers?

162
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:44,917
He was never

163
00:09:45,751 --> 00:09:46,836
affected by her powers.

164
00:09:46,919 --> 00:09:47,920
-What?
-What?

165
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:49,088
They didn't affect him?

166
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:52,758
Yeah, I guess not.

167
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:56,596
I don't care about her electrical powers.

168
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:59,348
I'm here because I want to be
with Ms. Na Bo-bae.

169
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:02,602
It's all I ever wanted, then and now.

170
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:04,604
Oh my.

171
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:08,357
I like this guy, then I don't,
and now I like him again.

172
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,568
A man shouldn't give up easily.

173
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:14,030
-Reminds me of my younger days.
-Gosh, Dad.

174
00:10:14,113 --> 00:10:15,781
Anyway, it's late.

175
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:18,075
We should let him stay the night,
don't you think?

176
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,660
I don't think so.

177
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,495
If he stays, he pays.

178
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:25,791
You run a lodging business,
so you should know how business works.

179
00:10:35,926 --> 00:10:36,802
PRECIOUS SHINE MUSCAT JAM

180
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,304
Pack 100 boxes before bed.

181
00:10:41,974 --> 00:10:43,434
A hundred boxes?

182
00:10:43,517 --> 00:10:45,645
This is my parents' main product.

183
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:48,230
Consider it payment for your stay.

184
00:10:49,273 --> 00:10:51,150
And do not go near Bo-bae's room.

185
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:54,278
I shall be keeping a close eye on you.

186
00:12:08,561 --> 00:12:09,854
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

187
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:11,856
Are you asleep?

188
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:26,036
Ms. Na,

189
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:29,248
I'll just talk to you from here.

190
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:34,837
I…

191
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:38,090
After you disappeared…

192
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:41,844
I really felt

193
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:45,431
like I was going to die.

194
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:50,436
For the first time…

195
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:55,983
I felt like I might die
because of someone else

196
00:12:57,818 --> 00:13:00,613
instead of my own heart.

197
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:05,284
I know you're doing this…

198
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:10,498
because you're worried…

199
00:13:13,292 --> 00:13:14,752
you might put me in danger.

200
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:19,924
If…

201
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:26,472
I really do end up in danger
because of your powers…

202
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:35,231
I'll find a way somehow.

203
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:41,570
Just don't tell me

204
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:44,490
to leave.

205
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,030
Bo-bae?

206
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,199
It's Mom.

207
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:34,665
What is it?

208
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:39,336
We didn't mean to,
but we heard everything.

209
00:14:41,255 --> 00:14:43,007
Your dad was moved to tears.

210
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,595
Shoot. You heard all that?

211
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:50,097
You could've covered your ears.

212
00:14:50,681 --> 00:14:53,726
Hey, it's not my fault
our walls are paper-thin.

213
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:56,812
You two could've gone outside to talk.

214
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,398
Or you could've texted. You have phones.

215
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:02,359
So what if you heard us?

216
00:15:04,695 --> 00:15:07,573
You're just happy
I have a boyfriend, right?

217
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:10,659
And thrilled my powers
may be gone for good, right?

218
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:12,786
Of course I'm happy.

219
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:17,207
I know how much
you've been struggling on your own.

220
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:25,716
We may know a lot
about your electrical powers,

221
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:29,345
but we can never know how you feel.

222
00:15:30,471 --> 00:15:31,972
How could we ever know

223
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:35,434
how scared and lonely you were…

224
00:15:37,978 --> 00:15:39,563
so young and all alone?

225
00:15:40,981 --> 00:15:41,815
Right?

226
00:15:43,275 --> 00:15:45,194
What's gotten into you?

227
00:15:48,697 --> 00:15:52,993
When you said you wanted to be a writer,
it broke my heart.

228
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:58,207
You must've wanted to write
because you had so much bottled up inside.

229
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:02,503
You must've been so lonely,
with no one to open up to,

230
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:04,797
that you had to pour it all onto paper.

231
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:08,050
So I'm happy.

232
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:09,969
I'm glad.

233
00:16:10,594 --> 00:16:13,764
That you now have someone to whisper to
and share things with.

234
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:23,816
Always choose the path

235
00:16:24,775 --> 00:16:26,485
that makes you happy.

236
00:16:27,736 --> 00:16:32,199
Whether you have electrical powers or not,
whether you're with someone or not,

237
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:35,160
wherever you are,

238
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:37,496
find something that makes you happy first.

239
00:16:39,456 --> 00:16:42,209
Then you'll be on the right path.

240
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:50,342
Gosh.

241
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:53,512
It's so nice

242
00:16:54,763 --> 00:16:57,099
to hold my daughter in my arms again.

243
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:04,106
Senior Managing Director Choi is here.

244
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:15,743
Mr. Yoon.

245
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:19,580
Hello.

246
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:21,040
Mr. Lee.

247
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:40,559
First-week coverage after launch
was 130% above our forecast.

248
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:43,645
Brand asset usage
was also highly effective.

249
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:45,355
How many major placements?

250
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:48,025
Thirty-two in total. I've shared the list.

251
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:49,485
Mr. Baek…

252
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:51,111
I mean…

253
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:55,282
Mr. Choi. Have you checked the list?

254
00:17:55,365 --> 00:17:56,617
No, I haven't.

255
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:59,203
I'm sure the employees did a good job.

256
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,996
TS pays them plenty.

257
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:03,540
Oh.

258
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:05,209
Of course.

259
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:14,176
Ms. Han, that color looks
really good on you today.

260
00:18:15,886 --> 00:18:17,304
What's your best color?

261
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:21,016
Mr. Choi Do-yoon, may I have a word?

262
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,780
-What are you doing?
-What do you mean?

263
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:38,033
I know you're excited to run TS Resort,
even if it's temporary.

264
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,451
But do your job properly--

265
00:18:39,535 --> 00:18:41,870
"Temporary"? Who said it's temporary?

266
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:43,038
What?

267
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:46,375
TS Resort, and eventually TS Group,
will be mine.

268
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,127
It's only a matter of time.

269
00:18:49,419 --> 00:18:51,088
I have my grandmother's support.

270
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:54,800
-I thought it was just until Mr. Baek--
-No.

271
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:56,844
I've been chosen.

272
00:18:57,886 --> 00:19:00,222
Do you know what Baek Ho-rang is up to?

273
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:02,516
He's looking for Na Bo-bae.

274
00:19:03,016 --> 00:19:06,395
He's been running all over the place,
completely lost.

275
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:10,232
TS doesn't care about him anymore.

276
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:14,069
Do you think someone like my grandmother
would take him back?

277
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:19,700
So that means I'm the official heir now.

278
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:24,872
You said you'd consider marrying me
if I became the heir to TS.

279
00:19:27,916 --> 00:19:28,959
Does that still stand?

280
00:19:43,348 --> 00:19:44,308
My gosh.

281
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:49,855
What are you doing so early?

282
00:19:49,938 --> 00:19:50,856
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

283
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,192
Good morning.

284
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:56,153
Are you still doing this?

285
00:19:56,236 --> 00:19:57,946
I finished the 100 boxes.

286
00:19:58,030 --> 00:20:00,616
Now I'm doing it as a form of meditation.

287
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:01,992
Don't mind me.

288
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:03,994
My son-in-law is good with his hands.

289
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:05,162
"Son-in-law"?

290
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:08,582
My son-in-law is a quick learner.
Just like his future father-in-law.

291
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:12,711
This is our farm's Insta.
Ho-rang made it for us.

292
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:14,129
"Ho-rang"?

293
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:17,132
Yeah, a great name.
Roar! Ho-rang, like "tiger."

294
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:20,093
An energetic name
that embodies the spirit of Korea.

295
00:20:20,177 --> 00:20:23,138
Listen, the person I respect most
is Baekbeom.

296
00:20:23,722 --> 00:20:26,433
He's quick with his hands
and has a head for business.

297
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:27,601
But…

298
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:30,103
Na Bo-bae.

299
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:33,190
How are your electrical powers?
It's been over 48 hours.

300
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:35,192
I still can't use them.

301
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:37,027
Wow, what's going on?

302
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:40,113
Mom! It's been over 48 hours.

303
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:42,074
-No way! Then…
-I know, right?

304
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:43,116
What's happening?

305
00:20:43,825 --> 00:20:46,245
-It's good if they stay gone.
-Forty-eight hours?

306
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:47,412
It's the first time.

307
00:20:47,496 --> 00:20:52,251
My electrical powers have never been gone
for more than 48 hours before.

308
00:20:52,751 --> 00:20:55,295
So what happens after 48 hours?

309
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:56,838
I don't know yet.

310
00:20:57,422 --> 00:21:00,008
It's been over 48 hours,
and your powers haven't returned.

311
00:21:00,842 --> 00:21:04,096
Doesn't that mean
your powers are gone for good?

312
00:21:05,013 --> 00:21:08,600
Well, I guess you could see it that way.

313
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:10,519
Ho-rang.

314
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:22,781
Mr. Lee told me to stock up
on healthy desserts.

315
00:21:22,864 --> 00:21:25,617
Sugar-free and gluten-free.

316
00:21:27,494 --> 00:21:29,246
Why can't he just eat whatever?

317
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:32,499
Ladies.

318
00:21:33,917 --> 00:21:37,254
You all know
what kind of person Mr. Baek is.

319
00:21:38,171 --> 00:21:39,256
He'll be back soon.

320
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,216
Of course.

321
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:44,886
Mr. Baek always has plans A to Z.

322
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:48,724
I'm sure he's already gearing up
to come back.

323
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:49,683
That's right.

324
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:55,314
Huh?

325
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:57,941
Mr. Yoon, Ms. Go.

326
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,985
Isn't this Mr. Baek?

327
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:02,029
Why is Mr. Baek here?

328
00:22:06,908 --> 00:22:08,577
#DMTOORDER #PRECIOUS #SHINEMUSCATJAM

329
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:09,661
#HEARTHEALTH #VITAMINS

330
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,079
Here, son-in-law.

331
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:12,289
Try this too.

332
00:22:12,372 --> 00:22:13,540
Thank you, Mother.

333
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:19,921
Our family knows how to reward hard work.
You worked hard, so eat your fill.

334
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,298
My tiger son-in-law.

335
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:22,716
Thank you.

336
00:22:23,925 --> 00:22:26,678
-I see you're addressing him differently.
-I know, right?

337
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:33,769
"The owner is so handsome"?

338
00:22:34,394 --> 00:22:36,021
I'm pretty good-looking myself.

339
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:38,065
Huh?

340
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:40,150
Ji-hye, what is this?

341
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:46,031
Looks like someone reposted it,
saying the guy in the picture is handsome.

342
00:22:46,615 --> 00:22:50,285
Once something like this goes viral,
people click right away.

343
00:22:50,369 --> 00:22:51,995
"Viral"? Is that a theme park ride?

344
00:22:52,579 --> 00:22:57,250
Oh, I noticed earlier that orders
for our jam have increased tenfold.

345
00:22:57,334 --> 00:22:58,335
Really?

346
00:22:58,418 --> 00:22:59,419
Son-in-law.

347
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:00,962
Can you pack a few more?

348
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:03,382
No problem, Mother.

349
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:07,010
Hey, you guys,
help my son-in-law pack the jam

350
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:10,389
while your dad and I are out
at the farm today, okay?

351
00:23:10,472 --> 00:23:11,306
Okay.

352
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:12,307
-Sure.
-Yeah.

353
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:14,935
Son-in-law, let's take another one.

354
00:23:15,852 --> 00:23:17,229
-Yeah. That's it.
-Me too.

355
00:23:19,272 --> 00:23:21,358
That's exactly how I looked
when I was young.

356
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:47,426
What on earth are you doing here, sir?

357
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:50,512
Do you know how dire things are
at TS Resort?

358
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:53,890
I told you I wouldn't go back
until I found her.

359
00:23:53,974 --> 00:23:56,685
But you found her.
You should come back now!

360
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:59,271
You have no idea how bad things are.

361
00:23:59,354 --> 00:24:00,730
Senior Managing Director Choi…

362
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:04,609
Choi Do-yoon is all excited
about marrying Director Han.

363
00:24:04,693 --> 00:24:07,028
Good for him. It's what he wanted.

364
00:24:07,112 --> 00:24:07,988
Sir.

365
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:09,114
"Sir"?

366
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:10,740
Who is…

367
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:15,120
Oh! These are Ms. Na Bo-bae's parents,

368
00:24:15,203 --> 00:24:20,083
the owners
of the Precious Shine Muscat Jam.

369
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:22,002
And this is her brother.

370
00:24:27,382 --> 00:24:29,801
Hello,
I'm Senior Managing Director Baek's--

371
00:24:30,635 --> 00:24:32,804
This is a friend of mine.

372
00:24:32,888 --> 00:24:34,598
I asked him to help us pack the jam.

373
00:24:34,681 --> 00:24:36,475
The more hands, the better, right?

374
00:24:37,392 --> 00:24:39,269
That's great!

375
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:41,897
You really know what you're doing.

376
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:43,023
See? I told you.

377
00:24:43,106 --> 00:24:45,400
He's a diamond in the rough,
but he'll go far.

378
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:46,860
A Siberian tiger!

379
00:24:46,943 --> 00:24:48,445
Roar!

380
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:49,946
We're off to the farm.

381
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:51,323
Okay. Take care.

382
00:24:52,073 --> 00:24:53,492
-Pack 'em up.
-Yes, sir.

383
00:25:05,003 --> 00:25:06,338
-Let's go inside.
-Sorry?

384
00:25:07,839 --> 00:25:08,798
Sir?

385
00:25:19,392 --> 00:25:21,645
Sir, are you really going to do this?

386
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:26,316
I'm not going back to Seoul
without Ms. Na Bo-bae.

387
00:25:26,399 --> 00:25:29,611
Why are you using me as an excuse?

388
00:25:30,111 --> 00:25:31,571
If Ms. Na stays,

389
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:33,865
I can stay here forever.

390
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:36,159
Sir.

391
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:39,037
Everyone's so desperate.

392
00:25:39,829 --> 00:25:41,456
What about your goal?

393
00:25:42,999 --> 00:25:45,502
Didn't you want to change TS Group?

394
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:47,295
Fold that corner properly.

395
00:25:48,255 --> 00:25:49,089
I'm sorry.

396
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,009
Bo-bae.

397
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:57,430
You know it's been well over 48 hours
since your powers stopped, right?

398
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:02,060
So what?

399
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:04,729
Nothing. Just saying.

400
00:26:07,524 --> 00:26:08,984
Hurry up and fold!

401
00:26:09,067 --> 00:26:10,860
We have to fill today's orders.

402
00:26:10,944 --> 00:26:12,487
Yes, sir.

403
00:26:22,497 --> 00:26:23,582
Come on in.

404
00:26:26,376 --> 00:26:27,877
President Baek, you're here too.

405
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:30,380
I thought it was just a meal with Do-yoon.

406
00:26:31,172 --> 00:26:32,090
Sit next to him.

407
00:26:39,681 --> 00:26:42,058
I heard you're looking
at wedding dresses tomorrow.

408
00:26:42,142 --> 00:26:43,351
I thought we should meet.

409
00:26:44,352 --> 00:26:45,478
Wedding dresses.

410
00:26:46,313 --> 00:26:47,147
Right.

411
00:26:49,357 --> 00:26:51,192
Do-yoon did say we should go look.

412
00:26:52,902 --> 00:26:55,363
How about we have
the formal family meeting this week?

413
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:57,282
It would just be your father, correct?

414
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,951
Is your stepmother still bed-bound?

415
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:02,787
Yes.

416
00:27:02,871 --> 00:27:05,707
Right. Well, the four of us
can have a simple meal,

417
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:07,584
book the venue, and set the date.

418
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:10,545
My husband can't make it anyway.

419
00:27:10,629 --> 00:27:13,298
Right. He's in prison.

420
00:27:14,215 --> 00:27:15,634
That's right.

421
00:27:16,384 --> 00:27:19,262
I mean,
you didn't have to put it so bluntly.

422
00:27:21,806 --> 00:27:22,724
Oh, right.

423
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:26,227
I heard Hanlim Advertising Company
is handling the Sterling project.

424
00:27:27,562 --> 00:27:32,108
You can help us with Sterling
and help steer TS.

425
00:27:32,192 --> 00:27:34,611
Just thinking about it makes me so happy.

426
00:27:34,694 --> 00:27:36,988
It paints a perfect picture, you know?

427
00:27:38,657 --> 00:27:42,077
Mom, do we have to talk about work here?

428
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:44,412
Aren't you getting ahead of yourselves?

429
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:45,330
Huh?

430
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:47,957
Senior Managing Director Baek Ho-rang, no…

431
00:27:48,041 --> 00:27:50,835
We don't know
how Mr. Baek Ho-rang will react.

432
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:56,257
I understand he had also been pushing
for the Sterling Group contract.

433
00:27:56,841 --> 00:27:58,927
But he isn't in Seoul right now.

434
00:27:59,552 --> 00:28:02,889
I heard he's working at some grape farm.

435
00:28:02,972 --> 00:28:04,307
He followed Na Bo-bae there.

436
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:07,060
Na Bo-bae?

437
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:09,229
Sir.

438
00:28:09,312 --> 00:28:10,438
You'll hurt your back.

439
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:12,857
Don't strain yourself.
I'll handle everything.

440
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:14,734
Thanks.

441
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:18,947
Hey, Ho-rang.

442
00:28:19,447 --> 00:28:20,490
Yes?

443
00:28:20,573 --> 00:28:22,117
You should go back to Seoul today.

444
00:28:25,203 --> 00:28:26,037
Sorry?

445
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:28,498
That man came all the way here
to find his boss.

446
00:28:29,499 --> 00:28:32,419
You can't just abandon your business,
even if it's hard.

447
00:28:34,295 --> 00:28:37,966
Finding Ms. Na Bo-bae was more important.

448
00:28:38,049 --> 00:28:39,843
I like that you put Bo-bae first.

449
00:28:40,885 --> 00:28:43,513
But now that I've started my own business,

450
00:28:43,596 --> 00:28:47,308
customers waiting for our jam
have moved up my priority list.

451
00:28:47,892 --> 00:28:51,479
Once they place an order,
they rely on me to fulfill it.

452
00:28:54,023 --> 00:28:56,234
A boss should never forget that.

453
00:28:57,235 --> 00:29:00,864
So you should go back and see it through,
win or lose.

454
00:29:02,532 --> 00:29:03,575
Go get 'em, Tiger.

455
00:29:13,585 --> 00:29:14,419
Let's go back.

456
00:29:17,255 --> 00:29:18,089
What?

457
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:21,593
This is the longest I've gone
without my powers.

458
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:22,844
It's a new record.

459
00:29:24,929 --> 00:29:27,766
It's my first time,
so I'm a little scared, but…

460
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:30,310
Let's go back to Seoul.

461
00:29:32,479 --> 00:29:33,396
Let's

462
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:35,440
go together.

463
00:29:37,776 --> 00:29:38,818
Are you serious?

464
00:29:38,902 --> 00:29:41,654
You said you'd die without me.

465
00:29:42,155 --> 00:29:44,449
That you feel at ease when you see me.

466
00:29:44,532 --> 00:29:46,451
I feel the same way.

467
00:29:46,534 --> 00:29:47,869
I

468
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:50,246
need you too.

469
00:29:52,332 --> 00:29:53,833
So let's go.

470
00:29:55,585 --> 00:29:58,463
Even if it's scary and new,

471
00:29:59,172 --> 00:30:00,006
let's go together.

472
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:10,433
Okay.

473
00:30:11,059 --> 00:30:12,060
Let's go.

474
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:15,688
Even if it's scary and new,

475
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:17,315
let's go together.

476
00:30:20,735 --> 00:30:22,529
What are you doing? Are you crazy?

477
00:30:22,612 --> 00:30:25,073
Don't hug her so tight!
You'll break her ribs.

478
00:30:25,156 --> 00:30:28,493
Should we look for a venue for them
while we prepare for your wedding?

479
00:30:28,576 --> 00:30:30,703
My gosh, Mom. Don't get carried away.

480
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:32,247
Hey, pull him off her.

481
00:30:32,747 --> 00:30:33,748
Why? They look good.

482
00:30:33,832 --> 00:30:35,124
Take care!

483
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:38,461
-Oh my!
-Bye!

484
00:30:38,962 --> 00:30:39,796
What?

485
00:30:40,296 --> 00:30:42,340
Could you please reconsider?

486
00:30:42,841 --> 00:30:44,926
You can't…

487
00:30:45,009 --> 00:30:47,345
All right. Understood.

488
00:30:58,314 --> 00:30:59,357
You're here, sir.

489
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:02,819
It's the end of the day. Why so tense?

490
00:31:03,319 --> 00:31:05,738
Well, the thing is…

491
00:31:06,281 --> 00:31:09,242
We got a call from Sterling, sir.

492
00:31:09,325 --> 00:31:12,120
As you know,
we have a meeting with them in a few days.

493
00:31:13,371 --> 00:31:16,416
They want to cancel it.

494
00:31:16,499 --> 00:31:19,168
Wasn't it a big deal?
Them expanding into Asia?

495
00:31:19,252 --> 00:31:20,378
They're canceling it?

496
00:31:20,461 --> 00:31:21,337
Yes.

497
00:31:21,421 --> 00:31:24,924
Isn't TS their exclusive partner?
What can they do without us?

498
00:31:25,508 --> 00:31:28,970
Well, they didn't cancel it altogether.

499
00:31:29,929 --> 00:31:31,431
They had one condition.

500
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:36,352
You recently became
the senior managing director.

501
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:41,941
They said they're open to meeting with you
after you've settled into your role.

502
00:31:42,025 --> 00:31:44,527
That's their condition.

503
00:31:56,289 --> 00:31:57,290
What?

504
00:31:57,373 --> 00:31:58,291
So…

505
00:32:00,293 --> 00:32:06,591
First, they want to see you demonstrate
what you're capable of, and then--

506
00:32:06,674 --> 00:32:07,967
Keep it simple.

507
00:32:09,010 --> 00:32:13,139
So they're canceling it
because I'm not Baek Ho-rang.

508
00:32:13,222 --> 00:32:14,682
No.

509
00:32:14,766 --> 00:32:18,144
That's not exactly what they said, but…

510
00:32:18,811 --> 00:32:20,813
Well, Senior Managing Director Baek is…

511
00:32:26,986 --> 00:32:28,613
"Senior Managing Director Baek"?

512
00:32:29,572 --> 00:32:31,741
Hey. Is he still
the senior managing director?

513
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:34,619
No, I misspoke. I'm sorry, sir.

514
00:32:35,912 --> 00:32:36,746
Get lost.

515
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:05,149
Ms. Han.

516
00:33:05,650 --> 00:33:08,486
The meeting with Sterling on the 23rd
has been canceled.

517
00:33:09,153 --> 00:33:11,322
They won't meet unless it's with Mr. Baek.

518
00:33:13,950 --> 00:33:14,784
Well…

519
00:33:15,535 --> 00:33:19,706
Could you please try to persuade him?

520
00:33:22,542 --> 00:33:25,420
He's holed up on some farm.
How am I supposed to persuade him?

521
00:33:25,503 --> 00:33:27,380
I spoke to Mr. Yoon earlier.

522
00:33:28,798 --> 00:33:30,258
He's coming back to Seoul today.

523
00:33:31,634 --> 00:33:32,468
What?

524
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:15,470
You left everything as it was?

525
00:34:16,095 --> 00:34:17,388
If I had cleaned it up,

526
00:34:18,723 --> 00:34:21,684
it would've felt like
you were really gone.

527
00:34:23,853 --> 00:34:27,315
And I wanted to leave a place
for you to come back to.

528
00:34:42,288 --> 00:34:45,625
Our contract's over, but there's one thing
left on my romance bucket list.

529
00:34:48,336 --> 00:34:51,798
It's your birthday party.
Are you sure you want to have it here?

530
00:34:53,174 --> 00:34:55,176
We could go somewhere else if you want.

531
00:34:55,259 --> 00:34:56,844
This is all I need.

532
00:34:56,928 --> 00:34:57,804
Still,

533
00:34:57,887 --> 00:35:01,724
your birthday passed while we were apart.

534
00:35:10,066 --> 00:35:11,651
Hurry up and sing for me.

535
00:35:11,734 --> 00:35:14,612
Happy birthday to you

536
00:35:14,695 --> 00:35:17,448
Happy birthday to you

537
00:35:17,532 --> 00:35:20,409
Happy birthday, dear Na Bo-bae

538
00:35:20,493 --> 00:35:23,037
Happy birthday to you

539
00:35:32,839 --> 00:35:36,634
Thank you, Mr. Baek Ho-rang,
for celebrating my 30th birthday with me.

540
00:35:38,553 --> 00:35:41,264
Now we've done everything
on my romance bucket list.

541
00:35:44,600 --> 00:35:45,685
Are you sure

542
00:35:46,519 --> 00:35:48,855
this is the last thing
on your bucket list?

543
00:35:50,398 --> 00:35:51,899
There's nothing else you want to do?

544
00:35:53,276 --> 00:35:54,610
There's a lot.

545
00:35:55,194 --> 00:35:56,779
There's so much I want to do.

546
00:35:57,280 --> 00:36:00,283
You'll do all those things with me, right?

547
00:36:02,577 --> 00:36:03,661
I'll think about it.

548
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:06,706
What's there to think about?

549
00:36:10,334 --> 00:36:12,336
Of course I'll do it with you.

550
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:15,381
You're the one I like.
Who else would I do it with?

551
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:22,805
The cream!

552
00:36:22,889 --> 00:36:24,724
Huh? The cream?

553
00:36:26,350 --> 00:36:27,560
Don't!

554
00:36:27,643 --> 00:36:29,478
No! Stop.

555
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:31,981
Oh! There's something I want to do.

556
00:36:47,038 --> 00:36:49,123
Are you ready for our date?

557
00:36:50,416 --> 00:36:52,877
Why are you watching me get ready?

558
00:36:59,508 --> 00:37:01,260
Seriously…

559
00:37:15,524 --> 00:37:17,735
Right. I'll have…

560
00:37:18,277 --> 00:37:20,947
I'll have Mr. Yoon bring the car.

561
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:23,991
Huh? Isn't he working right now?

562
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:25,451
Oh, is he?

563
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:29,497
And I want to take the bus or subway
instead of the car.

564
00:37:29,580 --> 00:37:30,706
Let's go somewhere busy.

565
00:37:31,415 --> 00:37:33,084
What? Why would you…

566
00:37:37,713 --> 00:37:40,424
I have a car, you know.

567
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:43,511
Come on, I want to go somewhere crowded.

568
00:37:49,892 --> 00:37:53,771
The doors are closing.

569
00:37:58,276 --> 00:37:59,443
Did you see that?

570
00:37:59,527 --> 00:38:01,821
So many people here,
and I didn't zap anyone.

571
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:05,908
That's cute! I want to check it out.

572
00:38:07,618 --> 00:38:09,078
-How do I look?
-You look silly.

573
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:14,041
You're such a dork.

574
00:38:15,167 --> 00:38:16,002
A dork?

575
00:38:17,253 --> 00:38:18,379
So pretty!

576
00:38:18,462 --> 00:38:19,422
Rawr!

577
00:38:19,505 --> 00:38:21,507
Mr. Baek, jiggle it.

578
00:38:23,092 --> 00:38:24,593
So cute!

579
00:38:25,803 --> 00:38:27,096
What are you doing?

580
00:38:36,355 --> 00:38:37,189
No, I'm good.

581
00:38:41,193 --> 00:38:42,695
It's too big.

582
00:38:42,778 --> 00:38:43,654
You can do it.

583
00:38:47,658 --> 00:38:48,868
Are you ready?

584
00:38:49,368 --> 00:38:50,911
-Let's do this.
-Okay.

585
00:38:57,793 --> 00:38:59,086
I have to say,

586
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:02,131
a normal date like this is fun.

587
00:39:02,214 --> 00:39:03,090
Yeah.

588
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:05,176
I never knew normal could be this nice.

589
00:39:21,150 --> 00:39:22,526
I'll meet you inside.

590
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:25,279
Yeah, you should talk to her.

591
00:39:34,538 --> 00:39:36,123
Door unlocked.

592
00:39:42,004 --> 00:39:44,173
You looked like you were dying,

593
00:39:44,256 --> 00:39:46,467
but you ended up coming back

594
00:39:47,551 --> 00:39:48,469
with Ms. Na.

595
00:39:48,552 --> 00:39:50,471
Without Ms. Na Bo-bae,

596
00:39:51,639 --> 00:39:53,557
I would have died.

597
00:39:54,683 --> 00:39:57,686
Why are you here, Ms. Han?

598
00:39:57,770 --> 00:39:59,355
I thought we were done talking.

599
00:40:02,149 --> 00:40:05,653
I'm here to talk business as the director
of Hanlim Advertising Company.

600
00:40:05,736 --> 00:40:08,030
Sterling Group canceled the meeting.

601
00:40:08,531 --> 00:40:11,158
They won't even negotiate
without you, so--

602
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:14,578
We have no reason to be involved now.
You're as pragmatic as I am,

603
00:40:14,662 --> 00:40:16,455
so let's settle things between us.

604
00:40:17,915 --> 00:40:20,835
You can cancel the contract
with TS Resort.

605
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:22,503
If you want,

606
00:40:22,586 --> 00:40:25,297
you can announce
that Hanlim pulled out first

607
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:26,799
and use me as an excuse.

608
00:40:29,301 --> 00:40:30,636
That's irresponsible of you.

609
00:40:33,055 --> 00:40:35,516
Am I supposed to thank you
for being considerate?

610
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:37,643
If this is because of personal reasons--

611
00:40:37,726 --> 00:40:38,769
No, it's not.

612
00:40:38,853 --> 00:40:42,440
I'm trying to take responsibility
for this situation.

613
00:40:49,405 --> 00:40:50,406
And

614
00:40:51,323 --> 00:40:52,533
I remember you.

615
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:55,327
More than ten years ago,

616
00:40:55,911 --> 00:40:58,164
a middle school kid
jumped in front of my car.

617
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:04,420
I might have been a savior to you
back then,

618
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:07,339
but to me,

619
00:41:08,883 --> 00:41:11,051
you seemed like someone
with a lot of scars,

620
00:41:11,552 --> 00:41:13,220
like my younger self.

621
00:41:13,804 --> 00:41:16,682
That's why I said what I said.

622
00:41:18,684 --> 00:41:21,061
To be honest, even now,

623
00:41:21,645 --> 00:41:24,523
I still see you as that kid
from back then.

624
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:26,942
I've changed.

625
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:28,861
Is that so?

626
00:41:29,570 --> 00:41:30,488
Looks to me

627
00:41:31,864 --> 00:41:33,240
like you're still hanging by a thread.

628
00:41:34,283 --> 00:41:35,826
From now on,

629
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:37,870
you have to really think about it.

630
00:41:38,537 --> 00:41:40,414
How to truly protect yourself.

631
00:41:41,790 --> 00:41:43,834
From Plan A to Plan Z.

632
00:41:44,627 --> 00:41:45,711
Be persistent.

633
00:42:13,447 --> 00:42:15,449
Why are you still out here?

634
00:42:19,078 --> 00:42:22,122
"Without Ms. Na Bo-bae,
I would have died"?

635
00:42:25,209 --> 00:42:26,502
You heard everything?

636
00:42:26,585 --> 00:42:28,003
I could hear everything.

637
00:42:28,087 --> 00:42:29,880
Even the part where you rejected her.

638
00:42:43,894 --> 00:42:46,146
When I heard him say
he would've died without me,

639
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:48,065
I realized something.

640
00:42:48,899 --> 00:42:52,903
It didn't matter whether I'd drained
all my powers saving Mr. Baek Ho-rang,

641
00:42:52,987 --> 00:42:56,448
or whether they'd come back again one day.

642
00:42:58,576 --> 00:43:02,204
Meeting him was a one-in-a-million chance,

643
00:43:02,288 --> 00:43:06,333
just like the lightning that struck me.

644
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:14,091
And I want to risk everything
to protect him.

645
00:43:23,267 --> 00:43:27,438
Just like he risked everything to love me.

646
00:43:27,938 --> 00:43:30,149
Electricity, charging, death.

647
00:43:30,733 --> 00:43:33,652
None of that ever mattered.

648
00:43:47,333 --> 00:43:48,500
So pretty.

649
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:04,099
You're here.

650
00:44:04,767 --> 00:44:06,018
You're an hour late.

651
00:44:06,101 --> 00:44:07,936
I heard Sterling canceled the meeting.

652
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:19,490
Try on a dress.

653
00:44:20,366 --> 00:44:21,659
By the way,

654
00:44:21,742 --> 00:44:25,287
I like seeing your neck and shoulders.

655
00:44:27,122 --> 00:44:30,584
Even with your new position,
you're still the same.

656
00:44:33,212 --> 00:44:35,381
Come on, let's stop talking about work.

657
00:44:36,006 --> 00:44:38,926
Let's talk about us. About our wedding.

658
00:44:39,009 --> 00:44:42,096
This is why you'll always be
in Baek Ho-rang's shadow.

659
00:44:44,640 --> 00:44:47,476
You don't hide your greed,
but your work is sloppy.

660
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:51,480
Han Seol-hee.

661
00:44:53,357 --> 00:44:55,526
Did you forget we're getting married?

662
00:44:55,609 --> 00:44:58,112
You expect me to risk my life
on someone like you?

663
00:44:59,488 --> 00:45:00,322
Marriage?

664
00:45:01,156 --> 00:45:02,157
Know your place.

665
00:45:03,617 --> 00:45:06,036
-Hey, Han Seol-hee.
-Are you crazy? Let go!

666
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:07,621
That hurts!

667
00:45:08,330 --> 00:45:11,875
Hey, how much longer
do I have to know my place?

668
00:45:12,501 --> 00:45:13,877
What is my place?

669
00:45:13,961 --> 00:45:15,546
What do you even know about me?

670
00:45:16,547 --> 00:45:18,090
-Let go!
-Sir, please calm down.

671
00:45:18,173 --> 00:45:19,633
Please calm down.

672
00:45:22,261 --> 00:45:23,804
Goddamn it.

673
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:28,308
Hey.

674
00:45:28,392 --> 00:45:29,935
Let's get you up.

675
00:45:30,436 --> 00:45:31,729
Han Seol-hee.

676
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:33,814
Han Seol-hee!

677
00:45:34,857 --> 00:45:35,858
Han Seol-hee!

678
00:45:39,820 --> 00:45:41,280
Sir, please calm down.

679
00:45:41,363 --> 00:45:42,656
-You can't do this.
-Move!

680
00:45:42,740 --> 00:45:43,782
Out of my way!

681
00:45:48,245 --> 00:45:49,747
Sir, you can't drive like this!

682
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:50,831
He shouldn't…

683
00:45:54,585 --> 00:45:58,005
Choi Do-yoon, I heard the Sterling meeting
got canceled. What's going on?

684
00:45:58,088 --> 00:45:58,922
Why?

685
00:45:59,506 --> 00:46:01,383
Are you going to blame me again?

686
00:46:01,467 --> 00:46:02,301
What?

687
00:46:02,885 --> 00:46:05,095
Do-yoon, have you been drinking?

688
00:46:05,179 --> 00:46:08,557
You're also like this
because I'm not Baek Ho-rang!

689
00:46:09,892 --> 00:46:13,020
Has anyone ever tried to listen
to what I think and feel?

690
00:46:13,604 --> 00:46:17,608
Mom, you know Do-yoon
won the fencing competition, right?

691
00:46:18,484 --> 00:46:20,360
Since Ho-rang is stuck in bed,

692
00:46:20,444 --> 00:46:23,113
Do-yoon brought his trophy to show him.

693
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:24,990
I'LL COME SEE YOU AFTER I FINISH UP
FROM MOM

694
00:46:25,073 --> 00:46:27,367
He's such a sweet boy, isn't he?

695
00:46:29,161 --> 00:46:30,746
Take out your trophy.

696
00:46:31,330 --> 00:46:32,623
Show it to Ho-rang.

697
00:46:33,248 --> 00:46:34,917
Yeah, take it out and show him.

698
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:46,053
It'll get in the way
when they change his IV.

699
00:46:47,429 --> 00:46:48,639
Put it on the floor.

700
00:46:56,355 --> 00:46:58,524
It was just a school fencing competition.

701
00:46:58,607 --> 00:47:01,193
She just wants to brag about Do-yoon,
Mother.

702
00:47:01,276 --> 00:47:06,240
I was supposed to go to my friend's today.
Now I'm stuck here because of you.

703
00:47:07,115 --> 00:47:09,201
You're so annoying.
I didn't ask you to come.

704
00:47:09,284 --> 00:47:12,037
I only came
'cause my mom and dad dragged me here.

705
00:47:13,038 --> 00:47:15,457
Can't you call your dad
and ask him to come quickly?

706
00:47:21,380 --> 00:47:22,548
Give it back.

707
00:47:26,385 --> 00:47:29,179
Auntie, Uncle.

708
00:47:30,222 --> 00:47:31,557
When will you be here?

709
00:47:32,808 --> 00:47:35,727
Ho-rang is in big trouble right now.

710
00:47:36,228 --> 00:47:37,646
Come quickly.

711
00:48:11,471 --> 00:48:14,224
TS GROUP VP IN CAR ACCIDENT

712
00:48:19,855 --> 00:48:21,940
TS GROUP VP AND WIFE FOUND DEAD IN CRASH

713
00:48:22,608 --> 00:48:24,860
I was just a child too!

714
00:48:25,360 --> 00:48:26,612
Just a scared child

715
00:48:26,695 --> 00:48:28,530
who wanted to run away!

716
00:48:30,282 --> 00:48:32,284
Why is it always my fault?

717
00:48:32,367 --> 00:48:34,494
Why am I always the troublemaker?

718
00:48:35,120 --> 00:48:38,874
If any of you cared for me
half as much as you did for Baek Ho-rang,

719
00:48:38,957 --> 00:48:42,044
my life wouldn't have turned out
this pathetic!

720
00:48:42,127 --> 00:48:43,921
Do-yoon. Choi Do-yoon!

721
00:48:44,004 --> 00:48:45,923
Where are you? You need to…

722
00:49:15,827 --> 00:49:20,082
I reported him for kidnapping
and spiking your drink.

723
00:49:20,165 --> 00:49:22,793
He was also arrested
for property damage at a wedding shop,

724
00:49:22,876 --> 00:49:26,296
drunk driving,
and assaulting a police officer.

725
00:49:27,130 --> 00:49:30,092
TS Hotel issued a statement
taking full responsibility

726
00:49:30,175 --> 00:49:32,928
and expressed their intention
to make things right.

727
00:49:33,762 --> 00:49:35,889
If this turns into a TS Group issue,

728
00:49:36,890 --> 00:49:39,935
my grandmother
won't let my aunt off the hook.

729
00:49:40,852 --> 00:49:42,229
Smart move.

730
00:49:45,565 --> 00:49:47,025
Change the nameplate back.

731
00:49:47,109 --> 00:49:49,111
As of today, my aunt and Choi Do-yoon

732
00:49:49,778 --> 00:49:50,988
are out of the picture.

733
00:49:52,823 --> 00:49:53,657
Yes, sir.

734
00:50:26,356 --> 00:50:29,026
I won't get in the way
of whatever you two choose to do.

735
00:50:30,068 --> 00:50:33,030
I know that trying to separate you
will only make you inseparable.

736
00:50:33,530 --> 00:50:34,364
But remember this.

737
00:50:36,033 --> 00:50:37,159
Just don't embarrass yourself.

738
00:50:37,993 --> 00:50:40,370
And don't think
your position is yours forever.

739
00:50:41,371 --> 00:50:42,205
Okay.

740
00:50:43,457 --> 00:50:44,875
Ma'am.

741
00:50:47,377 --> 00:50:50,881
May I say just one thing?

742
00:50:56,136 --> 00:50:59,014
You're worried about Mr. Baek Ho-rang,
aren't you?

743
00:50:59,931 --> 00:51:01,933
Can't you just be honest

744
00:51:02,017 --> 00:51:04,102
and tell him you're worried about him?

745
00:51:05,145 --> 00:51:07,230
I can see how worried you are

746
00:51:07,314 --> 00:51:08,940
from the way you look at him.

747
00:51:10,025 --> 00:51:13,028
I can see how much you care about him.

748
00:51:13,111 --> 00:51:16,406
But if you don't show it,
he won't know how you feel.

749
00:51:18,909 --> 00:51:22,662
And both you and Mr. Baek Ho-rang

750
00:51:22,746 --> 00:51:24,206
will end up hurting.

751
00:51:28,251 --> 00:51:29,461
Hi!

752
00:51:29,544 --> 00:51:31,630
Oh my, you're so cute.

753
00:51:31,713 --> 00:51:33,215
So adorable.

754
00:51:33,298 --> 00:51:35,175
I'll walk you to your car.

755
00:51:39,137 --> 00:51:40,764
You're so cute.

756
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:48,021
Your grandmother's the type to say no
when she disagrees, right?

757
00:51:49,606 --> 00:51:50,482
Yes.

758
00:51:51,983 --> 00:51:52,943
See?

759
00:51:53,026 --> 00:51:56,196
I told you she loves you very much.

760
00:51:56,696 --> 00:51:58,990
She just doesn't show it.

761
00:52:00,325 --> 00:52:01,243
Not true.

762
00:52:02,119 --> 00:52:03,995
She looks pretty baffled right now.

763
00:52:04,079 --> 00:52:06,998
I'm telling you, I'm right.

764
00:52:12,003 --> 00:52:13,171
Well…

765
00:52:14,381 --> 00:52:18,009
I sent your favorite tea

766
00:52:18,844 --> 00:52:21,721
and the Shine Muscat jam
to your secretary earlier.

767
00:52:22,389 --> 00:52:23,598
Please have some later.

768
00:52:23,682 --> 00:52:25,308
What's gotten into you?

769
00:52:25,976 --> 00:52:27,185
You even thought of me.

770
00:52:28,311 --> 00:52:30,856
Ms. Na Bo-bae told me to.

771
00:52:35,819 --> 00:52:36,736
So cute.

772
00:52:39,948 --> 00:52:41,533
What's your plan with her?

773
00:52:44,536 --> 00:52:46,830
I'll have some good news for you soon.

774
00:53:02,929 --> 00:53:04,931
The groom will now enter.

775
00:53:06,308 --> 00:53:08,351
A big round of applause, please.

776
00:53:33,084 --> 00:53:34,211
Cut!

777
00:53:34,294 --> 00:53:35,503
You scared me!

778
00:53:35,587 --> 00:53:36,755
-Let's roll.
-All good?

779
00:53:36,838 --> 00:53:39,090
You brat. You gonna ask me that
after every take?

780
00:53:39,174 --> 00:53:41,801
Nervous about your directorial debut,
Seo-jeong?

781
00:53:41,885 --> 00:53:42,928
Was it bad?

782
00:53:43,011 --> 00:53:45,430
The shot was shaky. Do another take.

783
00:53:47,390 --> 00:53:48,934
-Okay. That was good.
-Okay?

784
00:53:49,017 --> 00:53:51,770
-Why ask if you were gonna approve it?
-Just 'cause.

785
00:53:51,853 --> 00:53:53,647
-You're okay with a shaky shot?
-Yes.

786
00:53:53,730 --> 00:53:56,524
Caught a whiff of something sweet
among the shaking flowers?

787
00:53:56,608 --> 00:53:57,609
While walking…

788
00:53:57,692 --> 00:53:59,694
-Ms. Na, you're here.
-Na Bo-bae!

789
00:53:59,778 --> 00:54:01,404
-No traffic?
-Bo-bae!

790
00:54:01,488 --> 00:54:04,282
Oh, Ms. Na. You're here.

791
00:54:04,366 --> 00:54:06,534
Thanks so much for guest starring, Eun-ho.

792
00:54:06,618 --> 00:54:08,286
And you wouldn't even take a fee.

793
00:54:08,370 --> 00:54:10,872
It's an honor to be in your show.

794
00:54:11,498 --> 00:54:13,667
But I'm a little upset.

795
00:54:15,168 --> 00:54:17,879
I kept begging you
to let me play the lead.

796
00:54:17,963 --> 00:54:19,631
You can't play the lead.

797
00:54:19,714 --> 00:54:21,883
-Because you're my number one fan.
-True.

798
00:54:22,592 --> 00:54:26,304
I'm going to become a writer worthy
of being chosen by a top star like you,

799
00:54:26,388 --> 00:54:28,348
and not just because you're my fan.

800
00:54:30,058 --> 00:54:32,560
I guess I'll see you then.

801
00:54:32,644 --> 00:54:33,770
As writer and actor.

802
00:54:35,188 --> 00:54:38,441
Until then,
I'll keep guest starring in your shows

803
00:54:38,525 --> 00:54:40,652
and make sure you don't forget me.

804
00:54:41,528 --> 00:54:42,404
Na Bo-bae!

805
00:54:44,197 --> 00:54:47,659
We just shot
Eun-ho's wedding entrance scene.

806
00:54:47,742 --> 00:54:49,577
Is the shoot going well, Director Cho?

807
00:54:49,661 --> 00:54:52,622
I've been put through the wringer
under Director Yeom.

808
00:54:53,540 --> 00:54:54,916
Of course I nailed it.

809
00:54:55,834 --> 00:54:58,295
Put through the wringer? You?

810
00:54:58,378 --> 00:55:01,965
I taught you, guided you,
gave you love and joy. I did it all.

811
00:55:02,048 --> 00:55:03,258
-Oh! Thank you.
-"Oh"?

812
00:55:03,341 --> 00:55:05,719
-I heard you, okay?
-One sec. You little…

813
00:55:05,802 --> 00:55:07,887
Those two always crack me up.

814
00:55:17,397 --> 00:55:19,065
Ms. Na. Let's go.

815
00:55:23,194 --> 00:55:25,697
Ms. Na. Please sit here.

816
00:55:25,780 --> 00:55:27,699
It's been a while. You look great.

817
00:55:27,782 --> 00:55:30,160
Have some coffee, Secretary…
I mean, Ms. Na.

818
00:55:30,243 --> 00:55:32,996
You ladies are making me feel so awkward.

819
00:55:33,079 --> 00:55:35,749
My butt's a little sore.
Can I use this cushion?

820
00:55:35,832 --> 00:55:38,335
No need to feel awkward. You're a writer.

821
00:55:39,961 --> 00:55:40,879
Have a seat.

822
00:55:44,382 --> 00:55:45,884
Well, it's good.

823
00:55:45,967 --> 00:55:47,218
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

824
00:55:47,719 --> 00:55:50,847
Are you here to watch the shoot too?
Because I said I'd be here?

825
00:55:50,930 --> 00:55:53,683
Of course. I'm your fan, after all.

826
00:55:54,726 --> 00:55:57,020
And since we're shooting at TS Resort,

827
00:55:57,103 --> 00:55:59,606
I wanted to check on things as the owner.

828
00:55:59,689 --> 00:56:02,734
Man, this punk made me bring
a full A-to-Z plan

829
00:56:02,817 --> 00:56:06,821
when I asked for a location sponsorship
and made a damn fuss--

830
00:56:06,905 --> 00:56:09,282
You're yapping again.
Your blood sugar must be low.

831
00:56:09,991 --> 00:56:12,660
Yes, we'll get started now!

832
00:56:12,744 --> 00:56:13,995
Eun-ho, take that and…

833
00:56:14,579 --> 00:56:16,873
-I'm counting on you!
-Just roll already!

834
00:56:16,956 --> 00:56:18,917
-We'll start rolling!
-You're so loud.

835
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:21,252
Ready!

836
00:56:24,089 --> 00:56:24,923
Ready!

837
00:56:26,007 --> 00:56:27,300
Action!

838
00:56:27,884 --> 00:56:28,718
Shush.

839
00:56:34,808 --> 00:56:37,060
If I were the main character in a drama,

840
00:56:38,978 --> 00:56:41,314
this is how I'd be introduced.

841
00:56:46,945 --> 00:56:48,363
Name, Na Bo-bae.

842
00:56:48,947 --> 00:56:53,243
A woman over 30
with an uncertain future ahead of her.

843
00:56:56,663 --> 00:56:58,915
THE BODYGUARD IN MY HEART
WRITER NA BO-BAE

844
00:57:20,395 --> 00:57:23,857
WRITTEN BY NA BO-BAE

845
00:57:25,233 --> 00:57:27,402
My name! Did you see my name?

846
00:57:27,485 --> 00:57:30,780
But then again,
the future is always uncertain.

847
00:57:30,864 --> 00:57:31,865
Are you crying?

848
00:57:32,824 --> 00:57:33,658
I'm not.

849
00:57:35,827 --> 00:57:37,704
Something got in my eye.

850
00:57:37,787 --> 00:57:39,456
You're just so cute.

851
00:57:39,539 --> 00:57:40,748
And now,

852
00:57:40,832 --> 00:57:43,585
I have someone to walk hand in hand with
into that future.

853
00:57:43,668 --> 00:57:45,587
-So cute!
-What's with you?

854
00:57:50,383 --> 00:57:51,843
I just felt a tingle.

855
00:57:52,886 --> 00:57:53,887
Huh?

856
00:57:54,512 --> 00:57:55,430
Static electricity?

857
00:57:55,513 --> 00:57:56,723
Yes.

858
00:57:57,765 --> 00:57:58,600
But

859
00:57:59,601 --> 00:58:00,935
it didn't hurt.

860
00:58:05,482 --> 00:58:08,735
No matter who I am, as long as you love me

861
00:58:09,944 --> 00:58:13,072
and we can keep charging
each other forever,

862
00:58:13,656 --> 00:58:15,617
we can go anywhere.

863
00:58:17,076 --> 00:58:19,996
Together, always.

864
01:00:17,071 --> 01:00:21,701
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
